<% content_for :title, 'Subsector Build Plan' %>

<%= render 'help/page', title: 'Subsector Build Plan' do %>
  <div class='space-y-6'>
    <div>
      <dl class='space-y-5'>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Last Survey</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            Counts of star systems and rogue stellar objects currently present in the subsector.
            These will be replaced when Generate is confirmed.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Build Plan</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            YAML configuration controlling density, stellar composition, and fixed hex placements
            for the generated survey. See the
            <%= link_to 'build specification reference', help_page_path('subsector_build_specification'), class: 'no-underline hover:underline hover:underline-offset-2' %>
            for all available options.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Derive Build from Survey</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            <div class='space-y-3'>
              <p>The <span class="font-semibold text-fg-bright">Derive Build from Survey</span> button creates a build configuration
                that matches the existing sector data. This is useful when you want to generate a new version
                of the subsector but ensure that the same hexes have star systems and rogue objects.
              </p>
              <p>The derived build configuration preserves the structural outline of the subsector. It keeps:</p>
              <ul class='list-disc list-inside space-y-1'>
                <li>which hexes contain star systems</li>
                <li>the star types and the types of stellar bodies orbiting the stars</li>
                <li>the UWP for terrestrial planets</li>
                <li>the UWP for planetoid belts</li>
                <li>the size of gas giants</li>
                <li>which hexes contain rogue objects</li>
                <li>the types of rogue objects</li>
                <li>the names of objects</li>
              </ul>
              <p>Data that may change when generating the subsector will be the specific details about
                objects. For example, the atmospheric composition may be different, the number of moons or
                planetoids may change.</p>
            </div>
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Generate</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            Click this button to generate a new subsector survey using the configuration. Any existing star
            systems or rogue objects will be deleted.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Load Build Default</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            Opens the build default loader to replace this subsector's build configuration
            from TravellerMap, Deepnight, or an uploaded T5 file. See
            <%= link_to 'Load Build Default', help_page_path('subsectors_defaults_source'), class: 'no-underline hover:underline hover:underline-offset-2' %>
            for details.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Sector Grid</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            The map of subsectors in this sector. You can click on a subsector to view its survey record.
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class='pt-2 text-right uppercase font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.22em] text-fg-muted'>
      REFERENCE 0619SP
    </div>
  </div>
<% end %>
